course: dictionary
lesson: 16074
title: Waive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To waive something means to choose not to use it or not to ask for it. A waived fee is a fee you do not have to pay. This is a formal word, so you will often find it in letters, notices and rules.
explain: Read the clues in this sentence: «The club waived the joining fee for Sam because he was new to town.» The club did not ask Sam to pay, so waived must mean chose not to charge. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "The club chose not to charge the joining fee" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You can waive a rule, a fee or a right. For example: «The head teacher waived the rule about coats indoors because the heating had broken.» Waive sounds like wave, but they mean different things. A wave is a movement of your hand, and to waive is to let something go.
fact: Waive is a verb: waive, waives, waived, waiving.
fact: To waive means to choose not to use or demand something, such as a fee or a rule.
fact: «Waived» is the past tense, as in «The shop waived the delivery charge.»
fact: Waive sounds the same as wave, but the two words have different meanings.
fact: Waive is a formal word, so you will see it in letters, rules and notices more than in everyday talk.
exercise: «The shop waived the delivery charge, so we paid nothing extra.» What does waived mean here? | Wrapped up tightly | Made the bill bigger | *Chose not to charge | Waved hello to
exercise: Mia says, «The teacher waived the spelling test this week.» What does waive mean? | Made it harder | *Chose not to use it | Wrote it on the board | Waved at the class
exercise: Which word means to choose not to use a rule? | Wane | Wave | *Waive | Wavy
test: What does waived mean in «The gym waived its fee for new members this month»? | Made the fee bigger | *Did not ask for the fee | Waved at the new members | Wrote the fee down
test: Which word means a hand movement? Which word means to let a rule go? Pick the one that means to let a rule go. | Wavelength | Wave | Waver | *Waive
exam: Which word fits? The school ___ the late fee because the trip was cancelled. | Waiving | Wave | Waves | *Waived
